# Trivy vulnerability ignore list, read automatically by the scans in
# .github/workflows/trivy.yml (api scan ~line 87, web scan ~line 100).
#
# Rules for this file, so it never becomes the place risk goes to hide:
#   - one specific ID per entry, never a blanket or wildcard ignore
#   - every entry carries a date, the reason it cannot be fixed today, and
#     the concrete condition that unblocks it
#   - an entry that exists only to turn the gate green does not belong here;
#     fix the dependency instead
#   - re-check entries on every dependency upgrade, and delete them the
#     moment they resolve
#
# Everything else was fixed rather than ignored. For the record, on
# 2026-09-01 the two images went from 106 fixable HIGH/CRITICAL findings
# (7 of them CRITICAL) down to this single entry, by bumping the base images
# (python:3.12.11-slim -> 3.12.14-slim, node:22.11.0-slim -> 22.23.2-slim),
# deleting npm from the web runtime stage, and upgrading cryptography
# (49.0.0 -> 50.0.1) and next (16.2.10 -> 16.2.11).

# 2026-09-01 - sharp 0.34.5 in the web image. Fixed upstream in 0.35.0.
#
# Why it is not simply upgraded: next 16.2.11 declares sharp as an OPTIONAL
# dependency pinned to ^0.34.5, and that range excludes 0.35.0. Forcing it
# through an npm `overrides` entry would run sharp outside the range next
# supports. apps/web/app/opengraph-image.tsx genuinely uses next/image, so
# the cost is a broken Open Graph image pipeline - a real regression traded
# for a tidier scan result.
#
# Unblocked when next widens its sharp range to admit >= 0.35.0. Re-check on
# every next upgrade and delete this entry as soon as that lands.
GHSA-f88m-g3jw-g9cj
